zstd
Usage: zstd [-d] [-c] FILE   |   zstd -19 FILE

Compresses and decompresses zstandard streams -- the format the stick's images,
firmware and payloads arrive in, that nothing else here reads. Fast, and its
high levels squeeze hard.

	-d          decompress
	-c          write to stdout (pipe it on, e.g. `| tar xf -`)
	-19         a high compression level when packing

See also: file, tar
